concepts.content:
In a VAE, we encode an input, then decode it, and finally measure the reconstruction error between our original input and the output of the decoder. This process is analogous to a standard autoencoder. The relationship is shown in the likelihood calculation:

$$\begin{aligned}  
    \mu_x, \sigma^2_x &= g_{\theta}(z) & \quad\quad \triangleleft \quad\text{Decode $z$}&\\
    \log p_{\theta}(x | z) &= \log \mathcal{N}(x; \mu_x, \sigma^2_x) &\\
                          &= \log\frac{1}{\sigma_x\sqrt{2\pi}} - \frac{\overbrace{(x - \mu_x)^2}^{\text{reconstruction error}}}{2\sigma_x^2} & \quad\quad \triangleleft \quad\text{Measure likelihood}
\end{aligned}$$

